     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. A 1000 mg daily dose of sertraline is far above the 200 mg/day maximum. It could seriously harm the patient, and the order would be coming from someone who isn't the patient's prescriber.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Ask the treating prescriber to enter or confirm the order.** If they really want a dose this far outside the label, pharmacy and the clinical team can review it and document the reason.\n- **Send me a dose within the usual range**, such as 50 mg or 100 mg once daily, with confirmation from the prescriber. I'll enter that.\n- **If this is about something else**, such as a possible overdose or a policy question, I'd suggest involving the pharmacy or the medical director.\n\nI'm happy to help with any of these."
      }
     ],
